WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Step 1: Add the job. Top bar → Add a job

1b
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Paste the job link and your interview date. See what it needs, your resume match, the gaps and a plan.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Step 2: Tailor your resume. Your job → Resume tab → Tailor your resume

2b
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Rewrite your bullets for this job’s keywords, without inventing anything.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Step 3: Study the gaps. Resources → Study library

3b
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Free notes on every topic, linked from the gaps in your resume.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4: Answer this job’s questions. Practice → Questions for this job

4b
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Feedback quotes your own words. Try again and see each criterion improve.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Step 5: AI Interview Coach. Top bar → AI Coach

5b
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Any question, answered from your resume and stories, with every point labelled.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Step 6: Trade-off drills. Practice → Trade-off drills

6b
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Make a design call and hold it while the interviewer pushes back.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Step 7: Voice mock interview. Top bar → Mock interview

7b
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Answer out loud. Follow-ups on what you said, then content and delivery feedback.

8
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Step 8: Know when you’re ready. Top bar → Readiness

8b
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
One score per job and the day you’ll be ready, checked against your interview.

9
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Step 9: Interview notes and debrief. Your job → After the interview → Take notes

9b
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Type questions during the real interview. Afterwards they become your debrief.
